# Large binary copied from aihpc_val/tools/nvlmapper/dist_amd64 (NVLMAPPER / run_nvlmapper.sh)
bin/scripts/nvlmapper

# ---- Python / tooling ----
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
dist/
build/*
!build/README.md
.local/
.env

# ---- App runtime (regenerated; cluster-specific) ----
var/cache/
var/workflows/runs/
# Build identity, written into the image by the Dockerfile (app_version.py reads it). Committing
# one would pin every later checkout to a stale build string.
backend/build-info.json
# Catalog store (platforms/tools/projects; seeded on boot, cluster-specific)
var/store/
# Durable run/metric history (SQLite + WAL; created on boot by results_history.py)
var/history/
# Generated report archive (durable runtime data, never source).
var/reports/
# Runtime logs, including the agent tool-call audit trail (agent/audit.py)
var/logs/

# Generated reports kept for later download (report_store.py); operator artifacts, not source
var/reports/

# ---- Identity store (NEVER commit — SRP verifiers and revocation state) ----
#
# A verifier is not a password, but it is credential material: it is the value `srp` checks a proof
# against, and it is what an offline guessing attack runs against. The store also carries the
# revocation cutoffs, so a committed copy silently re-honours sessions a later deployment withdrew
# (INV-19 in identity-auth-traps.mdc).
#
# `NVIS_IDENTITY_FILE` defaults under var/identity/, and bin/run-local-auth.sh points at
# var/local-auth/, so both appear in a developer tree after the first local login.
var/identity/
var/local-auth/
**/identity.json

# ---- TLS material (NEVER commit — server.key is a private key) ----
#
# Phase 0.5 generates a self-signed pair here on first boot. Committing the key would publish the
# private half of every developer's certificate, and re-issuing is a one-line regeneration, so
# there is never a reason to track it.
var/tls/
**/*.key
**/*.pem
!**/*.pub.pem

# ---- Token vault (NEVER commit — encrypted NVFTP tokens + master key material) ----
var/secrets/
**/*.vault.json
**/*.vault.flock
**/.vault_master_key
**/.rack_web_secret_key

# ---- Demo report logs (extracted from reports.tar.gz) ----
demo-reports/

# Default rack / multirack comment store (override with RACK_COMMENTS_FILE)
rack_comments.json

# ---- Local export bundles (see README / handoff zips) ----
nvis-rack-status-cluster-export-*.zip
rack-web-cluster-export-*.zip

# ---- Saved Docker image bundles (build-docker.sh save) ----
nvis-rack-status-*.tar
nvis-rack-status-*.tar.gz
nvis-rack-status-*.tar.sha256
nvis-rack-status-*.tar.gz.sha256

# ---- Frontend (React SPA) ----
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
static/spa/
static/docs/
docs/_build/

# ---- Desktop shell (Electron) ----
# `release/` holds packaged installers -- a single macOS bundle is ~255 MB, so this is the one
# entry here that matters. `out/` is the tsc output the app actually runs. Neither is covered by
# the `dist/`-style patterns above, which is worth stating because the names differ deliberately:
# electron-builder's default output dir is `dist`, and it was pointed at `release` so that the
# 255 MB never lands in a directory the rest of this repo treats as disposable-but-tracked.
desktop/node_modules/
desktop/out/
desktop/release/
# tsc's incremental cache. Machine-specific absolute paths, so committing one makes another
# checkout's first build either wrong or a no-op.
*.tsbuildinfo

# ---- Manual snapshots taken before edits (foo.py.bak.<tag>) ----
*.bak
*.bak.*
*.bak-*
*.prebak.*

# ---- Deployment overrides and key material (plaintext credentials: keep local) ----
# docker-compose.override.yml carries RACK_WEB_AUTH_TOKEN / RACK_GRAFANA_PASSWORD
# and deploy-secrets/ holds an ssh key, so neither belongs in history.
docker-compose.override.yml
deploy-secrets/

# ---- OS / editor ----
.DS_Store
._*
*.zip
Thumbs.db
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
frontend/coverage/

# Third-party vendor manuals (Dell/NVIDIA PDFs etc). Keep them in Drive, not here: they are
# multi-MB, redistribution-restricted, and git history is permanent — a manual committed once
# is carried by every clone forever. Our own docs are markdown and tracked normally.
docs/*.pdf

# >>> Agentic PLC managed (.plc) >>>
# Generated by the Agentic PLC installer; edits inside this block are overwritten.
.plc/*
!.plc/
!.plc/profile.json
!.plc/templates.json
!.plc/templates/
!.plc/templates/*.md
!.plc/jira-templates/
!.plc/jira-templates/*.md
!.plc/requirements/
!.plc/requirements/*.md
!.plc/design/
!.plc/design/*.md
!.plc/test/
!.plc/test/*.md
!.plc/briefs/
!.plc/briefs/*.md
!.plc/waivers.toml
.plc/tools/
.plc/telemetry/
.plc/security/
.plc/briefs/*-evidence.jsonl
.plc/briefs/*-mr-description.md
plc-evidence.jsonl
# <<< Agentic PLC managed (.plc) <<<

# Keep these OUTSIDE the managed block above — the installer overwrites anything
# inside it. Re-opens .plc/security/ after the managed exclusion so the reviewed
# threat-model markdown is tracked while raw SecNemo/scanner JSON stays local.
# If a future installer run drops `.plc/security/` from the managed block, these
# three lines are what keep the raw output out; re-check them.
!.plc/security/
.plc/security/*
!.plc/security/threat-model-*.md

# Same reasoning for the validation reports, and outside the managed block for the same reason.
# These are the advisory output of plc-requirements-validation / plc-design-validation /
# plc-v-model-validate. Tracked deliberately: Keith asked for the requirements, design and test
# documents to be committed so the project's progress is visible over time, and a review that found
# 30 findings is part of that record -- a snapshot of what the documents looked like when reviewed.
# Run state (v-model-state.json) stays untracked; it is per-developer working state, not evidence.
!.plc/plc-requirements-validation-report.md
!.plc/plc-design-validation-report.md
!.plc/plc-v-model-validate-summary.md

# Agentic PLC skills are a per-developer local install (each dev runs the
# installer), not a work product. Our tracked agent guidance stays where it
# already lives: AGENTS.md, the CLAUDE.md symlink, and .cursor/rules.
.agents/
.claude/
.codex/

# Agent scratch space: intermediate command output, captured cluster inventories,
# test fixtures pulled off a head node. Currently ~2,000 files, none of them a work
# product. Untracked and unignored is the dangerous combination — one `git add .`
# commits the lot — so it is named here explicitly.
.scratch/

# Operator configuration. Only the generated example is tracked; the real file and any
# certificate are per-deployment and must not enter shared git history -- five clusters use
# this repo (cluster-deployments.mdc). Secrets are refused from the file at startup, but a
# site's hostnames and paths are still nobody else's business, and a TLS key is a secret.
config/*
!config/rackstatus.toml.example

# Runtime script tree. `script_tree.tree_root()` falls back to the repo root when
# RACK_REMOTE_BASE_PATH is unset, so a local deploy stages here. Build artifact, never source.
bin/scripts-tree/
